    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "1. Types of Urban Data"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Urban data is generated continuously from multiple sources within a city ecosystem."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "A. Based on Structure"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Type",
        "Description",
        "Example"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Structured Data",
          "Organized in rows/columns",
          "Traffic counts, census tables"
        ],
        [
          "Semi-Structured Data",
          "Partial structure (tags/keys)",
          "JSON from APIs, XML"
        ],
        [
          "Unstructured Data",
          "No predefined format",
          "Images, CCTV footage, social media"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "B. Based on Source"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Sensor Data (IoT):</strong> Traffic sensors, pollution monitors",
        "<strong>Administrative Data:</strong> Government records (tax, land use)",
        "<strong>Crowdsourced Data:</strong> Social media, citizen reports",
        "<strong>Geospatial Data:</strong> Maps, satellite imagery"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "C. Based on Time Dimension"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Static Data:</strong> Census, infrastructure maps",
        "<strong>Dynamic Data:</strong> Live traffic, weather updates"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "2. Data Formats"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Data format defines how data is stored and exchanged."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Common Formats:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Format",
        "Use Case",
        "Characteristics"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "CSV",
          "Tabular data",
          "Simple, lightweight"
        ],
        [
          "JSON",
          "APIs, web data",
          "Flexible, hierarchical"
        ],
        [
          "XML",
          "Data exchange",
          "Structured with tags"
        ],
        [
          "GeoJSON",
          "Spatial data",
          "Coordinates + attributes"
        ],
        [
          "Raster/Vector",
          "GIS systems",
          "Maps, satellite images"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "highlight",
      "text": "<span class=\"key-idea\">Key Insight:</span> Format selection affects: Storage efficiency, Processing speed, Interoperability."
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "3. Types of Databases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Databases are systems used to store, manage, and retrieve data efficiently."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Major Categories:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Type",
        "Description",
        "Example Use"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Relational (SQL)",
          "Table-based",
          "Transport records"
        ],
        [
          "NoSQL",
          "Flexible schema",
          "Social media data"
        ],
        [
          "Spatial Databases",
          "Geographic data",
          "GIS systems"
        ],
        [
          "Cloud Databases",
          "Scalable storage",
          "Smart city platforms"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "4. Relational Databases (RDBMS)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> A relational database organizes data into tables (relations) with rows and columns."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Key Concepts:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Table = Entity (e.g., Traffic Data)",
        "Row = Record",
        "Column = Attribute"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Example Table:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Vehicle_ID",
        "Location",
        "Speed"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "V101",
          "MG Road",
          "45"
        ],
        [
          "V102",
          "Indiranagar",
          "30"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Important Features:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "<strong>Primary Key:</strong> Unique identifier",
        "<strong>Foreign Key:</strong> Links between tables",
        "<strong>SQL (Structured Query Language):</strong> Used for querying"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Advantages:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "High consistency",
        "Structured storage",
        "Strong data integrity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Limitations:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Less flexible for unstructured data",
        "Scaling can be complex"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "5. Database Normalization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> Normalization is the process of organizing data to reduce redundancy and improve integrity."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Goals:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Eliminate duplicate data",
        "Ensure logical data dependencies",
        "Improve efficiency"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Example (Before Normalization):"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Student \"A\" repeated across ML and DB courses in a single row."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "After Normalization:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Table 1: Students (| Student_ID | Name |)",
        "Table 2: Courses (| Course_ID | Name |)",
        "Table 3: Enrollment (| Student_ID | Course_ID |)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Normal Forms:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "<strong>1NF:</strong> Remove repeating groups",
        "<strong>2NF:</strong> Remove partial dependencies",
        "<strong>3NF:</strong> Remove transitive dependencies"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "👉 <strong>Outcome:</strong> Cleaner database, faster queries, reduced anomalies."
    },
    {
      "type": "section_heading",
      "text": "6. NoSQL Databases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "<strong>Definition:</strong> NoSQL databases store data in non-tabular formats, allowing flexibility."
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Types:"
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "headers": [
        "Type",
        "Structure",
        "Example"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Document",
          "JSON-like",
          "MongoDB"
        ],
        [
          "Key-Value",
          "Pair-based",
          "Redis"
        ],
        [
          "Column-Family",
          "Column groups",
          "Cassandra"
        ],
        [
          "Graph",
          "Nodes & edges",
          "Neo4j"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Advantages:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Flexible schema",
        "Handles large-scale data",
        "Suitable for real-time applications"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "sub_heading",
      "text": "Limitations:"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "style": "unordered",
      "items": [
        "Less strict consistency",
        "Complex querying compared to SQL"
      ]
    },
